        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="NEW04" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Cornelia</forename>
                        <surname>Newton</surname>
                        <addName>née Boinville</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1816-09-02"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>There seems to be a clear link between the <persName key="NEW01">Newton</persName> entries and the Boinville entries. The editors of Mary Shelley's 
    <title>Journal</title> have Cornelia as the sister of Mrs Boinville (not to be confused with Cornelia Boinville, the Boinville's daughter who married Thomas Turner and was 
    at risk to Shelley at one point) and the wife of John Frank Newton. This means that entries for 'Newtons' include Mrs Newton.</p>
                        <p>Godwin notes her death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"><title>The Journals of Mary Shelley</title> ed Feldman and Scott-Kilvert (John Hopkins, Baltimore, 1987)  </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
